<section id="Ax1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">Appendix</h2>

</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 3.2. The Theoretical Edge: Why Gradients Carry More Information ‣ 3. Motivation and Theoretical Analysis ‣ Reading Between the Lines: Towards Reliable Black-box LLM Fingerprinting via Zeroth-order Gradient Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Before proving Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 3.2. The Theoretical Edge: Why Gradients Carry More Information ‣ 3. Motivation and Theoretical Analysis ‣ Reading Between the Lines: Towards Reliable Black-box LLM Fingerprinting via Zeroth-order Gradient Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we first introduce and prove a related lemma about the Fisher information of a random variable following a normal distribution, as follows.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_smallcaps ltx_title_theorem">Lemma 0 (Fisher Information for a Normal Distribution).</h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> be a random variable following a normal distribution with mean <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> and variance <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>, which are differentiable functions of a parameter <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>. The Fisher information of <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> is:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(12)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{X}(\theta)=\frac{1}{\sigma^{2}(\theta)}\left(\frac{\partial\mu(\theta)}{\partial\theta}\right)^{2}+\frac{1}{2\sigma^{4}(\theta)}\left(\frac{\partial\sigma^{2}(\theta)}{\partial\theta}\right)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{X}(\theta)=\frac{1}{\sigma^{2}(\theta)}\left(\frac{\partial\mu(\theta)}{\partial\theta}\right)^{2}+\frac{1}{2\sigma^{4}(\theta)}\left(\frac{\partial\sigma^{2}(\theta)}{\partial\theta}\right)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 0 (Fisher Information for a Normal Distribution). ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem ‣ Reading Between the Lines: Towards Reliable Black-box LLM Fingerprinting via Zeroth-order Gradient Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The probability density function of the normal distribution is:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(13)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(x;\theta)=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi\sigma^{2}(\theta)}}\exp\left(-\frac{(x-\mu(\theta))^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}(\theta)}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(x;\theta)=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi\sigma^{2}(\theta)}}\exp\left(-\frac{(x-\mu(\theta))^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}(\theta)}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">The log-likelihood function is:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(14)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log p(x;\theta)=-\frac{1}{2}\log(2\pi)-\frac{1}{2}\log(\sigma^{2}(\theta))-\frac{(x-\mu(\theta))^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}(\theta)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p(x;\theta)=-\frac{1}{2}\log(2\pi)-\frac{1}{2}\log(\sigma^{2}(\theta))-\frac{(x-\mu(\theta))^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}(\theta)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">The score function is the partial derivative of the log-likelihood with respect to <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(15)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial}{\partial\theta}\log p(x;\theta)=\frac{(x-\mu(\theta))}{\sigma^{2}(\theta)}\frac{\partial\mu(\theta)}{\partial\theta}+\frac{(x-\mu(\theta))^{2}-\sigma^{2}(\theta)}{2\sigma^{4}(\theta)}\frac{\partial\sigma^{2}(\theta)}{\partial\theta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial}{\partial\theta}\log p(x;\theta)=\frac{(x-\mu(\theta))}{\sigma^{2}(\theta)}\frac{\partial\mu(\theta)}{\partial\theta}+\frac{(x-\mu(\theta))^{2}-\sigma^{2}(\theta)}{2\sigma^{4}(\theta)}\frac{\partial\sigma^{2}(\theta)}{\partial\theta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">The Fisher information is the expectation of the square of the score. Squaring the score function and taking the expectation, the cross-product term will have an expectation of <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we only need to consider the expectation of the squared terms. Let <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=X-\mu(\theta)\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2}(\theta))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=X-\mu(\theta)\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2}(\theta))</annotation></semantics></math>, using the central moments of the normal distribution <math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[Z]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[Z]=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[(Z)^{2}]=\sigma^{2}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[(Z)^{2}]=\sigma^{2}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[(Z)^{4}]=3\sigma^{4}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[(Z)^{4}]=3\sigma^{4}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>, we get:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(16)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{X}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\frac{(Z)}{\sigma^{2}(\theta)}\frac{\partial\mu(\theta)}{\partial\theta}\right)^{2}\right]+\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\frac{(Z)^{2}-\sigma^{2}(\theta)}{2\sigma^{4}(\theta)}\frac{\partial\sigma^{2}(\theta)}{\partial\theta}\right)^{2}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{X}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\frac{(Z)}{\sigma^{2}(\theta)}\frac{\partial\mu(\theta)}{\partial\theta}\right)^{2}\right]+\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\frac{(Z)^{2}-\sigma^{2}(\theta)}{2\sigma^{4}(\theta)}\frac{\partial\sigma^{2}(\theta)}{\partial\theta}\right)^{2}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">For the first term, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E17X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(17)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\frac{(Z)}{\sigma^{2}(\theta)}\frac{\partial\mu(\theta)}{\partial\theta}\right)^{2}\right]=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\frac{(Z)}{\sigma^{2}(\theta)}\frac{\partial\mu(\theta)}{\partial\theta}\right)^{2}\right]=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{\sigma^{4}(\theta)}\left(\frac{\partial\mu(\theta)}{\partial\theta}\right)^{2}\mathbb{E}[(Z)^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{\sigma^{4}(\theta)}\left(\frac{\partial\mu(\theta)}{\partial\theta}\right)^{2}\mathbb{E}[(Z)^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E17Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{\sigma^{2}(\theta)}\left(\frac{\partial\mu(\theta)}{\partial\theta}\right)^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{\sigma^{2}(\theta)}\left(\frac{\partial\mu(\theta)}{\partial\theta}\right)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">For the second term, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E18X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="5" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(18)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\frac{(Z)^{2}-\sigma^{2}(\theta)}{2\sigma^{4}(\theta)}\frac{\partial\sigma^{2}(\theta)}{\partial\theta}\right)^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\frac{(Z)^{2}-\sigma^{2}(\theta)}{2\sigma^{4}(\theta)}\frac{\partial\sigma^{2}(\theta)}{\partial\theta}\right)^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E18Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{4\sigma^{8}(\theta)}\left(\frac{\partial\sigma^{2}(\theta)}{\partial\theta}\right)^{2}\mathbb{E}[((Z)^{2}-\sigma^{2}(\theta))^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>8</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{4\sigma^{8}(\theta)}\left(\frac{\partial\sigma^{2}(\theta)}{\partial\theta}\right)^{2}\mathbb{E}[((Z)^{2}-\sigma^{2}(\theta))^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E18Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{4\sigma^{8}(\theta)}\left(\frac{\partial\sigma^{2}(\theta)}{\partial\theta}\right)^{2}(\mathbb{E}[(Z)^{4}]-2\sigma^{2}(\theta)\mathbb{E}[(Z)^{2}]+\sigma^{4}(\theta))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>8</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{4\sigma^{8}(\theta)}\left(\frac{\partial\sigma^{2}(\theta)}{\partial\theta}\right)^{2}(\mathbb{E}[(Z)^{4}]-2\sigma^{2}(\theta)\mathbb{E}[(Z)^{2}]+\sigma^{4}(\theta))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E18Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18Xc.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{4\sigma^{8}(\theta)}\left(\frac{\partial\sigma^{2}(\theta)}{\partial\theta}\right)^{2}(3\sigma^{4}(\theta)-2\sigma^{4}(\theta)+\sigma^{4}(\theta))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>8</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{4\sigma^{8}(\theta)}\left(\frac{\partial\sigma^{2}(\theta)}{\partial\theta}\right)^{2}(3\sigma^{4}(\theta)-2\sigma^{4}(\theta)+\sigma^{4}(\theta))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E18Xd" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18Xd.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{2\sigma^{4}(\theta)}{4\sigma^{8}(\theta)}\left(\frac{\partial\sigma^{2}(\theta)}{\partial\theta}\right)^{2}=\frac{1}{2\sigma^{4}(\theta)}\left(\frac{\partial\sigma^{2}(\theta)}{\partial\theta}\right)^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>8</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{2\sigma^{4}(\theta)}{4\sigma^{8}(\theta)}\left(\frac{\partial\sigma^{2}(\theta)}{\partial\theta}\right)^{2}=\frac{1}{2\sigma^{4}(\theta)}\left(\frac{\partial\sigma^{2}(\theta)}{\partial\theta}\right)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.7.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, we get:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(19)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{X}(\theta)=\frac{1}{\sigma^{2}(\theta)}\left(\frac{\partial\mu(\theta)}{\partial\theta}\right)^{2}+\frac{1}{2\sigma^{4}(\theta)}\left(\frac{\partial\sigma^{2}(\theta)}{\partial\theta}\right)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{X}(\theta)=\frac{1}{\sigma^{2}(\theta)}\left(\frac{\partial\mu(\theta)}{\partial\theta}\right)^{2}+\frac{1}{2\sigma^{4}(\theta)}\left(\frac{\partial\sigma^{2}(\theta)}{\partial\theta}\right)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.8.1" class="ltx_text">This completes the proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 0 (Fisher Information for a Normal Distribution). ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem ‣ Reading Between the Lines: Towards Reliable Black-box LLM Fingerprinting via Zeroth-order Gradient Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Given Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 0 (Fisher Information for a Normal Distribution). ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem ‣ Reading Between the Lines: Towards Reliable Black-box LLM Fingerprinting via Zeroth-order Gradient Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we then provide the proof of Theorem <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem ‣ Reading Between the Lines: Towards Reliable Black-box LLM Fingerprinting via Zeroth-order Gradient Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_smallcaps ltx_title_theorem">Theorem 2.</h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=f(WX+K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=f(WX+K)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is neither a linear nor an affine function, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> are constants with <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=\mathrm{d}Y/\mathrm{d}X=Wf^{\prime}(WX+K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\mathrm{d}Y/\mathrm{d}X=Wf^{\prime}(WX+K)</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose that <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> follows a zero-mean normal distribution, denoted as <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma_{X}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma_{X}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime\prime}(K)\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime\prime}(K)\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Under the first-order Taylor approximation, the Fisher information of <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(20)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{D}(W)\geq(\frac{c_{1}^{2}}{2W^{2}c_{2}^{2}\sigma_{X}^{2}}+4)\cdot\mathcal{I}_{Y}(W)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{D}(W)\geq(\frac{c_{1}^{2}}{2W^{2}c_{2}^{2}\sigma_{X}^{2}}+4)\cdot\mathcal{I}_{Y}(W).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}=f^{\prime}(K),c_{2}=f^{\prime\prime}(K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}=f^{\prime}(K),c_{2}=f^{\prime\prime}(K)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem ‣ Reading Between the Lines: Towards Reliable Black-box LLM Fingerprinting via Zeroth-order Gradient Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first analyze the Fisher information of <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=WX+K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=WX+K</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma_{X}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma_{X}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, the random variable <math id="A1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> is also normally distributed with mean <math id="A1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{Z}(W)=K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{Z}(W)=K</annotation></semantics></math> and variance <math id="A1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{Z}^{2}(W)=W^{2}\sigma_{X}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{Z}^{2}(W)=W^{2}\sigma_{X}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. We can now use Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 0 (Fisher Information for a Normal Distribution). ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem ‣ Reading Between the Lines: Towards Reliable Black-box LLM Fingerprinting via Zeroth-order Gradient Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> to calculate <math id="A1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{Z}(W)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{Z}(W)</annotation></semantics></math> with the parameter <math id="A1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta=W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta=W</annotation></semantics></math>. The partial derivatives of the mean and variance of <math id="A1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> are:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(21)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mu(W)}{\partial W}=0\quad\text{and}\quad\frac{\partial\sigma^{2}(W)}{\partial W}=2W\sigma_{X}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mu(W)}{\partial W}=0\quad\text{and}\quad\frac{\partial\sigma^{2}(W)}{\partial W}=2W\sigma_{X}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting these into the formula from Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 0 (Fisher Information for a Normal Distribution). ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem ‣ Reading Between the Lines: Towards Reliable Black-box LLM Fingerprinting via Zeroth-order Gradient Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E22X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(22)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{I}_{Z}(W)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{I}_{Z}(W)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sigma^{2}(W)}\left(\frac{\partial\mu(W)}{\partial W}\right)^{2}+\frac{1}{2\sigma^{4}(W)}\left(\frac{\partial\sigma^{2}(W)}{\partial W}\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sigma^{2}(W)}\left(\frac{\partial\mu(W)}{\partial W}\right)^{2}+\frac{1}{2\sigma^{4}(W)}\left(\frac{\partial\sigma^{2}(W)}{\partial W}\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E22Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{W^{2}\sigma_{X}^{2}}*0^{2}+\frac{1}{2(W^{2}\sigma_{X}^{2})^{2}}(2W\sigma_{X}^{2})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{W^{2}\sigma_{X}^{2}}*0^{2}+\frac{1}{2(W^{2}\sigma_{X}^{2})^{2}}(2W\sigma_{X}^{2})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E22Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{4W^{2}\sigma_{X}^{4}}{2W^{4}\sigma_{X}^{4}}=\frac{2}{W^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>X</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>X</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{4W^{2}\sigma_{X}^{4}}{2W^{4}\sigma_{X}^{4}}=\frac{2}{W^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=f(Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=f(Z)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of the parameter <math id="A1.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>, according to the Data Processing Inequality (DPI), the amount of information in data does not increase after any processing that is independent of the parameters. Therefore, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(23)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{Y}(W)\leq\mathcal{I}_{Z}(W)=\frac{2}{W^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{Y}(W)\leq\mathcal{I}_{Z}(W)=\frac{2}{W^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">Then, we analyze the Fisher information of <math id="A1.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=Wf^{\prime}(WX+K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=Wf^{\prime}(WX+K)</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A1.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>. Expand <math id="A1.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> about <math id="A1.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=K</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(24)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}(Z)=c_{1}+c_{2}(Z-K)+R_{2}(Z)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}(Z)=c_{1}+c_{2}(Z-K)+R_{2}(Z),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}:=f^{\prime}(K),c_{2}=f^{\prime\prime}(K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}:=f^{\prime}(K),c_{2}=f^{\prime\prime}(K)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.p4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{2}(Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{2}(Z)</annotation></semantics></math> is the Taylor remainder. Neglecting the remainder term <math id="A1.p4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> (this is the first-order approximation), and using <math id="A1.p4.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z-K=WX" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z-K=WX</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain the approximate linear form as follows:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(25)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\approx D_{\mathrm{approx}}:=c_{1}W+c_{2}W^{2}X." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>≈</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>approx</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\approx D_{\mathrm{approx}}:=c_{1}W+c_{2}W^{2}X.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">Under this approximation, <math id="A1.p4.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{approx}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>approx</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{approx}}</annotation></semantics></math> follows a normal distribution <math id="A1.p4.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(\mu_{D}(W),\sigma^{2}_{D}(W))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(\mu_{D}(W),\sigma^{2}_{D}(W))</annotation></semantics></math> because <math id="A1.p4.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> also follows a normal distribution.
From Eq. (<a href="#A1.E25" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem ‣ Reading Between the Lines: Towards Reliable Black-box LLM Fingerprinting via Zeroth-order Gradient Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>), we can calculate the mean and variance of <math id="A1.p4.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{approx}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>approx</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{approx}}</annotation></semantics></math> as functions of <math id="A1.p4.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E26X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(26)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E26X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mu_{D}(W):=\mathbb{E}[D_{\mathrm{approx}}]=Wc_{1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>approx</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mu_{D}(W):=\mathbb{E}[D_{\mathrm{approx}}]=Wc_{1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E26Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E26Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sigma^{2}_{D}(W):=\operatorname{Var}(D_{\mathrm{approx}})=W^{4}c_{2}^{2}\sigma_{X}^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>approx</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sigma^{2}_{D}(W):=\operatorname{Var}(D_{\mathrm{approx}})=W^{4}c_{2}^{2}\sigma_{X}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.7.1" class="ltx_text">since <math id="A1.p4.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[X]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[X]=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p4.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}(X)=\sigma_{X}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}(X)=\sigma_{X}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Differentiate the mean and variance w.r.t. <math id="A1.p4.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E27X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(27)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mu_{D}(W)}{\partial W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mu_{D}(W)}{\partial W}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=c_{1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=c_{1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E27Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial\sigma^{2}_{D}(W)}{\partial W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial\sigma^{2}_{D}(W)}{\partial W}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=4W^{3}c_{2}^{2}\sigma_{X}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=4W^{3}c_{2}^{2}\sigma_{X}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.8.1" class="ltx_text">Invoking Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 0 (Fisher Information for a Normal Distribution). ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem ‣ Reading Between the Lines: Towards Reliable Black-box LLM Fingerprinting via Zeroth-order Gradient Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> with the parameter <math id="A1.p4.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta=W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta=W</annotation></semantics></math>, mean <math id="A1.p4.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{D}(W)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{D}(W)</annotation></semantics></math> and variance <math id="A1.p4.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}_{D}(W)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}_{D}(W)</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain the Fisher information of the approximate normal model:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E28X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="4" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(28)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{I}_{D}(W)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{I}_{D}(W)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\frac{1}{\sigma^{2}_{D}(W)}\Big(\frac{\partial\mu_{D}(W)}{\partial W}\Big)^{2}+\frac{1}{2\sigma^{4}_{D}(W)}\Big(\frac{\partial\sigma^{2}_{D}(W)}{\partial W}\Big)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>D</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\frac{1}{\sigma^{2}_{D}(W)}\Big(\frac{\partial\mu_{D}(W)}{\partial W}\Big)^{2}+\frac{1}{2\sigma^{4}_{D}(W)}\Big(\frac{\partial\sigma^{2}_{D}(W)}{\partial W}\Big)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E28Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{c_{1}^{2}}{W^{4}c_{2}^{2}\sigma_{X}^{2}}+\frac{1}{2\,W^{8}c_{2}^{4}\sigma_{X}^{4}}\,\Big(4W^{3}c_{2}^{2}\sigma_{X}^{2}\Big)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>8</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>X</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{c_{1}^{2}}{W^{4}c_{2}^{2}\sigma_{X}^{2}}+\frac{1}{2\,W^{8}c_{2}^{4}\sigma_{X}^{4}}\,\Big(4W^{3}c_{2}^{2}\sigma_{X}^{2}\Big)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E28Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{c_{1}^{2}}{W^{4}c_{2}^{2}\sigma_{X}^{2}}+\frac{8}{W^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{c_{1}^{2}}{W^{4}c_{2}^{2}\sigma_{X}^{2}}+\frac{8}{W^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E28Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{2}{W^{2}}(\frac{c_{1}^{2}}{2W^{2}c_{2}^{2}\sigma_{X}^{2}}+4)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{2}{W^{2}}(\frac{c_{1}^{2}}{2W^{2}c_{2}^{2}\sigma_{X}^{2}}+4).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.9.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, we have the following conclusion: in this approximation,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(29)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{D}(W)\geq(\frac{c_{1}^{2}}{2W^{2}c_{2}^{2}\sigma_{X}^{2}}+4)\cdot\mathcal{I}_{Y}(W)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{D}(W)\geq(\frac{c_{1}^{2}}{2W^{2}c_{2}^{2}\sigma_{X}^{2}}+4)\cdot\mathcal{I}_{Y}(W).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.10.1" class="ltx_text">This completes the proof of Theorem <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem ‣ Reading Between the Lines: Towards Reliable Black-box LLM Fingerprinting via Zeroth-order Gradient Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Implementation Details</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Introduction to </span><span id="A2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">LeaFBench</span><span id="A2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span> <span id="A2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">LeaFBench</span> is a benchmark that facilitates a unified evaluation of LLM fingerprinting methods <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shao et al., 2025a</a>)</cite>. It includes 7 base model lineages, including Qwen2.5-7B, Qwen2.5-14B, Llama3.1-8B, Mistral-7B-v0.3, Gemma-2-2B, TinyLlama-1.1B-v1.0, and Llama-2-7B. <span id="A2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">LeaFBench</span> also implements 13 different post-development techniques that may be adopted to adjust the pre-trained base models. These techniques can significantly affect the behavior of the LLMs. These techniques include: <span id="A2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(1)</span> pretraining, <span id="A2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(2)</span> instructional tuning, <span id="A2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(3)</span> fine-tuning, <span id="A2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(4)</span> parameter-efficient fine-tuning, <span id="A2.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(5)</span> quantization, <span id="A2.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(6)</span> model merging, <span id="A2.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(7)</span> distillation, <span id="A2.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(8)</span> general-purpose system prompts, <span id="A2.p1.1.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(9)</span> role-playing system prompts, <span id="A2.p1.1.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(10)</span> chain-of-thought prompts, <span id="A2.p1.1.16" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(11)</span> sampling strategies, <span id="A2.p1.1.17" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(12)</span> retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), <span id="A2.p1.1.18" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(13)</span> adversarial manipulation. <span id="A2.p1.1.19" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">LeaFBench</span> includes a total number of 149 model instances.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Detailed Settings for </span><span id="A2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ZeroPrint</span><span id="A2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span> To generate the base queries, we sample code snippets from HumanEval, take the first 20 words, and then prepend them with “Complete the following code:” to form a query for a completion task. When conducting word substitutions, we use GloVe <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Pennington et al., 2014</a>)</cite> as the word embedding model. For each base query, we randomly replace 3 words with one of the top-10 similar words. The example queries are shown in Figure <a href="#A2.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Appendix B Implementation Details ‣ Reading Between the Lines: Towards Reliable Black-box LLM Fingerprinting via Zeroth-order Gradient Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and the pseudocodes of query set construction and fingerprint generation in <span id="A2.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ZeroPrint</span> are in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Appendix B Implementation Details ‣ Reading Between the Lines: Towards Reliable Black-box LLM Fingerprinting via Zeroth-order Gradient Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>&amp;<a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Appendix B Implementation Details ‣ Reading Between the Lines: Towards Reliable Black-box LLM Fingerprinting via Zeroth-order Gradient Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. The coefficient <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> in Ridge Regression is set to <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.001</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.001</annotation></semantics></math>. In our experiments, we utilize NVIDIA RTX 4090 GPUs with a total of 96GB VRAM.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F4" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.F4.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="385.22" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 231.98 385.22" width="231.98"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,385.22) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(115.99,0) translate(0,189.15)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#BFBFBF;--ltx-fill-color:#F6F6F6;" fill="#F6F6F6" fill-opacity="1" stroke="#BFBFBF" stroke-opacity="1"><path d="M 110.18 188.88 L -110.18 188.88 C -113.23 188.88 -115.71 186.4 -115.71 183.34 L -115.71 -183.34 C -115.71 -186.4 -113.23 -188.88 -110.18 -188.88 L 110.18 -188.88 C 113.23 -188.88 115.71 -186.4 115.71 -183.34 L 115.71 183.34 C 115.71 186.4 113.23 188.88 110.18 188.88 Z M -115.71 -188.88"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1" stroke="#000000" stroke-opacity="1" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -107.41 168.12)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:22.19em;--ltx-fo-height:0.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:25.2em;font-size:10pt;" height="355.42" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.73)" width="307.05"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.F4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:22.19em;">
<span id="A2.F4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"></span>
<span id="A2.F4.pic1.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.F4.pic1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;">Base Query:<span id="A2.F4.pic1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> 
<br class="ltx_break">Complete the following code: def will_it_fly(q,w): ”’ Write a function that returns True if the object q will fly, and False otherwise. The object … 
<br class="ltx_break">
