<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_figure ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="alg1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> <span id="alg1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ZeroPrint</span> Query Set Construction</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{source}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{source}</annotation></semantics></math>: Source dataset for base queries (<math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e.g." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e.g.</annotation></semantics></math>, HumanEval)

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>: Number of base queries to select

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>: Number of perturbed queries to generate per base query

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>: Number of words to replace in each perturbation

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>: Number of top semantically similar candidates to consider for replacement

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{word}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{word}</annotation></semantics></math>: Pre-trained word embedding model (<math id="alg1.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e.g." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e.g.</annotation></semantics></math>, GloVe)

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>: The query set containing base and perturbed queries

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
            
            
          
</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
            
            
          <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{base}\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{base}\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l11.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Initialize set for base queries
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
            
            
          <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l12.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Initialize the final query set
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\leftarrow 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\leftarrow 1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l13.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span> <span id="alg1.l13.5" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Select n base queries
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}\leftarrow\text{SampleAndFormat}(D_{source})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>SampleAndFormat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}\leftarrow\text{SampleAndFormat}(D_{source})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l14.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> e.g., “Complete the code: [snippet]”
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">15:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{base}\leftarrow Q_{base}\cup\{x_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{base}\leftarrow Q_{base}\cup\{x_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">16:</span></span>
            
            
          <math id="alg1.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q\leftarrow Q\cup Q_{base}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q\leftarrow Q\cup Q_{base}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l16.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Add all base queries to the final set
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">17:</span></span>
            
            
          
</div>
<div id="alg1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l18.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">18:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each base query <math id="alg1.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}\in Q_{base}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}\in Q_{base}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l18.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l19.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">19:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\leftarrow 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\leftarrow 1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l19.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span> <span id="alg1.l19.5" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Generate m perturbed versions
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l20.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">20:</span></span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime}_{i,j}\leftarrow x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime}_{i,j}\leftarrow x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l20.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Create a copy of the base query
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l21.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">21:</span></span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{replaceable}\leftarrow\text{SelectRandomWords}(x_{i},r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>SelectRandomWords</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{replaceable}\leftarrow\text{SelectRandomWords}(x_{i},r)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l21.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Select r words to replace
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l22.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">22:</span></span>
            
            
             <span id="alg1.l22.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each word <math id="alg1.l22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in W_{replaceable}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in W_{replaceable}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l22.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l23" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l23.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">23:</span></span>
            
            
               <math id="alg1.l23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{candidates}\leftarrow E_{word}.\text{TopKSimilar}(w,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mtext>TopKSimilar</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{candidates}\leftarrow E_{word}.\text{TopKSimilar}(w,k)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l23.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Find top-k similar words
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l24" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l24.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">24:</span></span>
            
            
               <math id="alg1.l24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{replacement}\leftarrow\text{RandomChoice}(C_{candidates})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>RandomChoice</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{replacement}\leftarrow\text{RandomChoice}(C_{candidates})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l25" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l25.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">25:</span></span>
            
            
               <math id="alg1.l25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime}_{i,j}\leftarrow\text{ReplaceWord}(x^{\prime}_{i,j},w,w_{replacement})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>ReplaceWord</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime}_{i,j}\leftarrow\text{ReplaceWord}(x^{\prime}_{i,j},w,w_{replacement})</annotation></semantics></math>
   
</div>
<div id="alg1.l26" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l26.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">26:</span></span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q\leftarrow Q\cup\{x^{\prime}_{i,j}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q\leftarrow Q\cup\{x^{\prime}_{i,j}\}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l26.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Add the perturbed query to the final set
  </span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l27" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l27.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">27:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l27.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg1.l27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_figure ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="alg2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> <span id="alg2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ZeroPrint</span> Fingerprint Generation</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
            
            
           <span id="alg2.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>: The target black-box LLM

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{base}=\{x_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{base}=\{x_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>: Set of base queries

</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{pert}=\{\{x^{\prime}_{i,j}\}_{j=1}^{m}\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{pert}=\{\{x^{\prime}_{i,j}\}_{j=1}^{m}\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>: Set of perturbed queries

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{sent}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{sent}</annotation></semantics></math>: Pre-trained sentence embedding model

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>: Number of times to query the model for each input to average outputs

</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg2.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>: Regularization hyperparameter for Ridge Regression

</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
            
            
           <span id="alg2.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg2.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>: The final fingerprint (aggregated Jacobian matrix) for model

</div>
<div id="alg2.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
            
            
          
</div>
<div id="alg2.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
            
            
          <math id="alg2.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{list}\leftarrow[]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{list}\leftarrow[]</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l11.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Initialize list to store local Jacobians
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg2.l12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each base query <math id="alg2.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}\in Q_{base}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}\in Q_{base}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l12.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg2.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta X_{i},\Delta Y_{i}\leftarrow[],[]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta X_{i},\Delta Y_{i}\leftarrow[],[]</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l13.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Initialize lists for input/output differences
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg2.l14.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Get stable embedding for the base query’s output
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">15:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg2.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{y_{i,k}\}_{k=1}^{t}\leftarrow\text{QueryModelMultipleTimes}(\mathcal{M},x_{i},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>QueryModelMultipleTimes</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{y_{i,k}\}_{k=1}^{t}\leftarrow\text{QueryModelMultipleTimes}(\mathcal{M},x_{i},t)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">16:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg2.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{e}_{y_{i}}\leftarrow\frac{1}{t}\sum_{k=1}^{t}E_{sent}(y_{i,k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{e}_{y_{i}}\leftarrow\frac{1}{t}\sum_{k=1}^{t}E_{sent}(y_{i,k})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">17:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg2.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{x_{i}}\leftarrow E_{sent}(x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{x_{i}}\leftarrow E_{sent}(x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l18.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">18:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg2.l18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each perturbed query <math id="alg2.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="alg2.l18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l18.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l19.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">19:</span></span>
            
            
             <span id="alg2.l19.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Get stable embedding for the perturbed query’s output
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l20.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">20:</span></span>
            
            
             <math id="alg2.l20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{y^{\prime}_{i,j,k}\}_{k=1}^{t}\leftarrow\text{QueryModelMultipleTimes}(\mathcal{M},x^{\prime}_{i,j},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>QueryModelMultipleTimes</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{y^{\prime}_{i,j,k}\}_{k=1}^{t}\leftarrow\text{QueryModelMultipleTimes}(\mathcal{M},x^{\prime}_{i,j},t)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l21.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">21:</span></span>
            
            
             <math id="alg2.l21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{e}_{y^{\prime}_{i,j}}\leftarrow\frac{1}{t}\sum_{k=1}^{t}E_{sent}(y^{\prime}_{i,j,k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{e}_{y^{\prime}_{i,j}}\leftarrow\frac{1}{t}\sum_{k=1}^{t}E_{sent}(y^{\prime}_{i,j,k})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l22.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">22:</span></span>
            
            
             <math id="alg2.l22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{x^{\prime}_{i,j}}\leftarrow E_{sent}(x^{\prime}_{i,j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{x^{\prime}_{i,j}}\leftarrow E_{sent}(x^{\prime}_{i,j})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l23" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l23.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">23:</span></span>
            
            
             <span id="alg2.l23.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Calculate input and output embedding differences
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l24" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l24.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">24:</span></span>
            
            
             <math id="alg2.l24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta x_{i,j}\leftarrow e_{x^{\prime}_{i,j}}-e_{x_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta x_{i,j}\leftarrow e_{x^{\prime}_{i,j}}-e_{x_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l25" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l25.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">25:</span></span>
            
            
             <math id="alg2.l25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta y_{i,j}\leftarrow\bar{e}_{y^{\prime}_{i,j}}-\bar{e}_{y_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta y_{i,j}\leftarrow\bar{e}_{y^{\prime}_{i,j}}-\bar{e}_{y_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l26" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l26.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">26:</span></span>
            
            
             Append <math id="alg2.l26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta x_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta x_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg2.l26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta X_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta X_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l27" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l27.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">27:</span></span>
            
            
             Append <math id="alg2.l27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta y_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta y_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg2.l27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta Y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta Y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>
  
</div>
<div id="alg2.l28" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l28.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">28:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg2.l28.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Estimate the local Jacobian using Ridge Regression
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l29" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l29.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">29:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg2.l29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{i}\leftarrow\arg\min_{J}\sum_{j=1}^{m}||\Delta y_{i,j}-J\Delta x_{i,j}||_{2}^{2}+\alpha||J||_{F}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msubsup><mrow><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mi>J</mi><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{i}\leftarrow\arg\min_{J}\sum_{j=1}^{m}||\Delta y_{i,j}-J\Delta x_{i,j}||_{2}^{2}+\alpha||J||_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l30" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l30.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">30:</span></span>
            
            
            Append <math id="alg2.l30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg2.l30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{list}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{list}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l31" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l31.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">31:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg2.l31.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Aggregate local Jacobians to form the final fingerprint
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l32" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l32.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">32:</span></span>
            
            
          <math id="alg2.l32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\mathcal{M}}\leftarrow\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}J_{list}[i]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\mathcal{M}}\leftarrow\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}J_{list}[i]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l33" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l33.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">33:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg2.l33.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg2.l33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{M}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Detailed Settings for the Baseline Fingerprinting Methods.</span> In our experiments, we take 1 white-box method and 4 state-of-the-art black-box methods as our baseline. For fair comparison, following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2025b</a>)</cite>, we also set the query limit to <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=200" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=200</annotation></semantics></math> while applying these methods. The detailed settings are as follows.</p>
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">REEF</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2025b</a>)</cite>: REEF is a forward-pass white-box fingerprinting method that relies on the intermediate representations as fingerprints. We strictly follow the original setting and sample 200 queries from TruthfulQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lin et al., 2022</a>)</cite> as the input queries.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LLMmap</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Pasquini et al., 2025</a>)</cite>: LLMmap is an untargeted black-box fingerprinting method. We adopt the 8 carefully-crafted prompts as the input queries and utilize the pre-trained open-set feature extraction model provided in its open-source repository.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MET</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gao et al., 2025</a>)</cite>: MET is also a untargeted black-box fingerprinting method that uses text completion prompts as input queries. The original MET uses 25 samples. Therefore, we run MET 8 times, leading to a total of 200 queries.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SEF</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shao et al., 2025a</a>)</cite>: SEF is an untargeted black-box fingerprinting method that straightforwardly uses the sentence embeddings of the outputs. Following original setting, we use Qwen3-Embedding-4B as the sentence embedding model and sample 200 queries from four different datasets, DROP <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dua et al., 2019</a>)</cite>, Ethics <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hendrycks et al., 2021</a>)</cite>, PubMedQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jin et al., 2019</a>)</cite>, and HumanEval <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2021</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">TRAP</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gubri et al., 2024</a>)</cite>: TRAP is a targeted black-box fingerprinting method that leverages GCG <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zou et al., 2023</a>)</cite> to generate targeted query-response pairs. For each query, we use GCG to optimize 100 iterations.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Detailed Settings of Ablation Studies.</span> For the ablation study of different query data, except the HumanEval dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2021</a>)</cite>, we select four other datasets as the source of the base queries, including the generative QA dataset TruthfulQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lin et al., 2022</a>)</cite>, the extractive QA dataset SQuAD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rajpurkar et al., 2016</a>)</cite>, the complicated reasoning QA dataset DROP <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dua et al., 2019</a>)</cite>, and a text completion dataset Wikipedia <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Foundation, [n. d.]</a>)</cite>. For the Wikipedia dataset, similar to HumanEval, we sample a text snippet with 20 words and prepend a completion instruction (<math id="A2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i.e." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i.e.</annotation></semantics></math>, “Continue the following text:”) to construct a completion prompt. For the ablation study of different sentence embedding models, we select the following 5 models: all-mpnet-base-v2 (MPNet), all-MiniLM-L6-V2 (MiniLM) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Reimers and Gurevych, 2019</a>)</cite>, potion-multilingual-128M (Model2Vec) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tulkens and van Dongen, 2024</a>)</cite>, Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B (Qwen3) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2025a</a>)</cite>, and EmbeddingGemma-300m (EmbeddingGemma) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schechter Vera et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. They are all classic or state-of-the-art sentence embedding models with different embedding dimensions.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Detailed Settings of Adaptive Attacks.</span> For input paraphrasing attacks, we utilize three small LLMs: Qwen2-0.5B-Instruct <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Team, 2024b</a>)</cite>, OLMo-2-0425-1B-Instruct <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">OLMo, 2024</a>)</cite>, and Gemma-2-2b-it <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Team, 2024a</a>)</cite>, to rewrite the input queries. The experiments of adaptive attacks are conducted on Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct and Llama3.1-8B-Instruct models.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Detailed Settings of the Overhead Evaluation.</span> The overhead evaluation is conducted on four derivative models from the Qwen2.5-7B lineage. For fair comparison, we utilize 1 NVIDIA RTX 4090 48GB GPU to compute the runtime of these LLM fingerprinting methods.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Ethic Statement</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The unauthorized usage of LLM has raised significant concerns about copyright infringements, while LLM fingerprinting offers a promising solution. In this paper, we propose a novel black-box fingerprinting method, <span id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ZeroPrint</span>. Our method is designed for the purely defensive purpose of copyright auditing and does not introduce new threats or vulnerabilities. Furthermore, our work utilizes publicly available datasets, such as HumanEval, for query construction and does not infringe on the privacy of any individual. The research does not involve any human subjects. As such, this work does not raise any major ethical issues.</p>
</div>
</section>
</article>
</div>
